  "executive_summary": "Across 25 detected updates, 25 items were assessed relevant to climate and actuarial risk, concentrated on general, mitigation energy, biodiversity nature.\n\nCategory analysis: Adaptation Resilience (1): Media Resilience and Risk Communication ; Biodiversity Nature (1): Philanthropy Key Change Climate Action; Catastrophe Natcat (3): WHO is on the Ground in Nepal Responding, 2026 Rasuwa Flash Floods; Climate Disclosure (1): IFRS S2 Climate-related Disclosures; Conference (1): Strengthening Urban Resilience and Disas; General (14): Environmental and Social Sustainability , 2026 Triple Cop Year Business; Health Mortality (1): The Climate and Health Risk Index; Mitigation Energy (1): Carbon Dioxide Removal CDR Market Infras; Parametric Insurance (1): Developing Parametric Insurance for Weat; Regulation Standards (1): Climate risk - International Association.\n\nActuarial implications include: general climate and actuarial evidence; energy-transition assumptions in pricing and asset strategies; nature-related risk factors in physical-risk frameworks.\n\nWorking-group follow-ups: review general items, review mitigation energy items, review biodiversity nature items."
